course: dictionary
lesson: 7539
title: Precise words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A precise word is exact. It says exactly what you mean, so the reader does not have to guess. «We had a nice cake at the nice party and it was nice» tells us nothing, but «a sticky cake» paints a picture.
explain: Precise can also mean very careful. In maths and science you are asked to be precise with a ruler or a thermometer, which means reading the exact number with the right units. Writers work the same way with words.
explain: Piling up words like «big, huge, enormous, massive, giant» does not make your writing precise. It just makes the reader wait for the point. Choose the one word that fits best.
explain: To test a word, swap a general word such as nice, good or big for your precise word. If the picture is clearer, you have chosen well.
fact: Precise means exact and correct in every small detail.
fact: Precise also means very careful and accurate when you do something.
fact: «At that precise moment» means exactly that moment, not roughly around it.
fact: «To be precise» tells the listener that the exact detail is coming next.
fact: Precise words give a clearer picture than general words like nice, good, big or bad.
exercise: Which word paints the clearest picture of a cake? | *lemony | good | nice | big
exercise: «The rocket took off at that precise moment.» What does precise mean here? | Very quickly | *Exactly that moment | Sometime that day | Very loudly
exercise: Which sentence gives precise instructions? | Do whatever feels nice | Walk somewhere near the park, sort of | *Turn left at the red postbox, then walk 20 steps | Just go over there and be good
test: Which answer gives a precise reading on a thermometer? | nice weather | *21.5 degrees Celsius | quite hot | warm
test: Which sentence uses precise words? | It was a bad thing | It was a good day | *The bus was late by exactly eight minutes | The big thing was really big
exam: The dog ran to the big tree. Which precise word could replace big tree? | good | *oak | bad tree | nice tree
